From 0ea6e275faddf0390ecd70a6f95c1b23a4fec8c6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Angelo Arifi <arifilabs@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 19 Sep 2026 12:07:03 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] feat(vulkan,lane-254 R66): three default flips - q5_K route
 on AMD, iq3 sign-hoist everywhere, iq3 n=7 rows on RDNA3

President ruling 2026-09-18: a proven-safe gain ships ON, including a gain that
shows nothing on our GPU. Each flip KEEPS its environment switch, so the legacy
arm stays selectable out of one binary, and each prints one startup line naming
the arm it chose and where the choice came from (probe vs override).

(a) GGML_ARIFI_Q5K_MMVQ: default `route` on AMD, `legacy` elsewhere.
    The Q5_K arm of ggml_vk_should_use_mmvq() already sits inside
    `vendor_id == VK_VENDOR_ID_AMD && n > 1`, so the device test is the one the
    predicate applies; no new device-detection path was added. Basis: R64's
    6-round paired table on 17408x5120, marginal q5_K column over n=4..8
    113.8 -> 5.4 us, 6/6 rounds won at n=5..8, recomputed by CHECK-R64-FABLE
    2 and 3. The k <= 8192 gate is kept EXACTLY as measured - at k=17408 the
    same route is a 0/6 LOSS at n=5. PPL at batch 8 is identical inside one
    stderr (5.9918 legacy vs 5.9932 route, +/-0.143). Non-AMD is unmeasured and
    keeps legacy; the registry row says so.

(b) GGML_ARIFI_IQ3_MMVQ: default `v2` on ALL devices.
    Bit-identical sha-for-sha: one deterministic dump sha over 76 executed cases
    per arm (iq3_s + iq3_xxs, n=1..10 and 64) is equal for legacy, a same-arm
    control and v2. 1229 -> 349 SPIR-V instructions per column. There is NO
    wall-clock change on gfx1103 (6 rounds, 0.991-1.013) because this driver's
    compiled stats are identical between the arms - the AMD compiler already
    hoists the loop-invariant select (CHECK-R61-FABLE F3). It ships for the
    drivers that do not hoist.

(c) GGML_ARIFI_IQ3_N7_ROWS: default 2 on AMD RDNA3 (is_rdna3), unset elsewhere.
    At NUM_COLS == 7 the inherited shape spills - raw scratchMemUsageInBytes 768
    at n=7 and 0 at every other width - and the pipeline costs ~462,000 us/run
    against ~20,900 with 2 rows; the rows=4 arm reproduces the cliff and is the
    control. The spill is a driver-allocator effect measured on this device
    class only, hence the device scope (CHECK-R61-FABLE (b) gate 4). The value
    reaches the iq3_s AND iq3_xxs f32 and f16 mat-vec pipelines (F5); the
    MUL_MAT_ID mirrors take rm_iq with NUM_COLS fixed at 1 and can never see it.
    CHECK-R61-FABLE F6 asked for a startup log line for this variable, which had
    none - it is added here.

Registry: the three rows carry the new defaults and their device scope, the
23.8x headline on the N7_ROWS row is struck for the 6-round 22.1x (F7), and the
two R65 switches that shipped UNREGISTERED (CHECK-R65-FABLE gate G1) are
registered - GGML_ARIFI_MMVQ_WIDE and GGML_ARIFI_MMVQ_WIDE_ROWS_FROM, both
diagnostic, both pointing at the closed lever mmvq-width-knee-capacity.

Origin: fork-authored (ArifiLabs lane-254 R66 integration, Opus 5 maker)
Measured-effect: UNMEASURED by the maker - integration; HQ measures the served chain
Lane: lane-254
Recut-onto: 668641bc0 (ArifiLabs lane-254 R66c, from 4908ce3cf)
